# STM32F446 Bare-Metal Starter Template

A lightweight, zero-HAL C project template for developing embedded firmware on the STM32F446 (ARM Cortex-M4) microcontroller. Designed as a clean starting point for bare-metal projects using GNU toolchains and OpenOCD.

## Features
* **Zero HAL / Direct Register Access:** Pure CMSIS-based target headers (`inc/`) and lightweight peripheral drivers (`src/rcc.c`).
* **Custom Startup & Linker Script:** Bare-metal startup assembly (`startup/`) and explicit memory layout management (`linker_script.ld`).
* **Automated Build & Flash:** Pre-configured `Makefile` for compiling, generating ELF/HEX outputs, and programming via OpenOCD.

## Prerequisites
Ensure the following tools are installed in your environment (Linux/WSL):
* `arm-none-eabi-gcc` toolchain
* `make`
* `openocd` (with debug probe pass-through configured)

## Repository Structure

.
├── inc/                # CMSIS core & STM32F446 register definitions
├── src/                # Application code and drivers
├── startup/            # Core vector table and initialization assembly
├── build/              # Generated target outputs (.elf, .hex)
├── obj/                # Compiled object files (.o)
├── linker_script.ld    # Flash and RAM memory configuration
└── Makefile            # Build and flash instructions

1. **Clone/Template:**
   ```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/] github link my-new-project
   cd my-new-project

Build Firmware: 
    make

Flash to target MCU:
    make flash

Clean build directory:
    make clean
